From 3598ae1faa8704dae92e6613aabf41f613231877 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 11:43:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Put the order button within reach and ask the form for
 less
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measured on a 390×844 phone: the product page ran 1820px and the ЗАХИАЛАХ
button sat at 1187px, 1.8 screens below the fold. The order form ran
1856px with ten boxes, eight of them demanded — entrance and door number
included, which a ger district or a countryside address does not have, and
the form stopped there with "fill in Орц".

Product page: a bar fixed to the foot of the screen carries the price and
ЗАХИАЛАХ while the real button is out of view, and steps aside when it is
in view (the bar's own band is excluded from that test, or the button would
surface behind it). It also gives way while the gallery's arrows or dots
sit in its band — a tap on a dot there would otherwise land on the order
button; measured on a 390×520 viewport, where the dots start under it. It
respects the safe-area inset, is not drawn for a sold-out product, and is
not drawn at all in the wide layout, where the button stays beside the
photos. Under the button: one line saying how they pay and whom to ring,
and a "call to order" link on the same number the sheet lists. No Messenger
link — no Facebook page handle exists anywhere in the sheet, the config or
the notes; one can be added beside the call link when it does.

Order form: six boxes, three demanded — name, phone, district or sum. City
and one free line for the rest of the address are optional; the call that
confirms every order fills in whatever is missing. Name and phone come
first, then delivery and payment, then the address, and one form wraps
both columns so Enter and the keyboard's "next" work across all of it. The
address reaches the sheet as "city, district, rest". Code.gs is untouched:
computeOrder_ already required only the phone and the slug, and still
prices the order from the sheet — checked with a stub, a client-sent unit
of 1 comes back as 119,000.

Measured after: bar on screen at load at 390×844 and 390×600, clear of the
gallery controls, hidden with the button in view; form 1781px, 6 boxes,
3 required; empty, name-only and name+phone submissions each name their
field, and name+phone+district goes through.

